# shir_nodes/char_extract.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# Extract characters/bytes by position (lowered from `cut -cN` / `cut -bN`).
#
# Backends: Perl substr(), JS slice(), C pointer arithmetic, Rust chars().skip()
# Fallback: sh2.charExtract(text, positions, byte_mode)
#
# ShIR_TextOps_Strings proves `char_extract_sound`: one contiguous start/length
# window over BYTES — the value is `take len (drop start s)`, never longer than
# `len` or than the input, empty for a zero length or an offset at/past the end,
# contiguous in the input (`s = r @ window @ z`) and invented from nothing
# (`set` inclusion). OUT OF MODEL: (1) character semantics — `cut -c` counts
# CHARACTERS, so with multi-byte UTF-8 the byte window differs and can return a
# bare continuation byte (`[195, 169, 97]` at 1/1 is `[169]`); `byte_mode = false`
# therefore needs a character-aware arm and is not promised by this model.
# (2) `cut`'s -d, comma lists and open ranges are several nodes or a lowering
# concern, not this one window. (3) negative offsets.

node CharExtract
tag "CharExtract"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field text: expr
field byte_mode: bool
spec: TextOps#char_extract_sound
